course: dictionary
lesson: 9827
title: Old words, new meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words change meaning over time. Old books may use a word that means something different today, so you need to read the clues around it. «Words change meaning: "meat" once meant any food, which is why old books say "meat and drink" and a "sweetmeat" is a sweet.» The clue is in the word itself: sweet and meat together make a sweet treat.
explain: Feasts in old stories often had «a plate of sweetmeats». If the sweetmeats came at the end of a feast, they were probably a treat for after the main meal. Ask yourself: what would fit in this place in the story? Then test your idea in the sentence.
explain: Today we say sweets in the UK, candy in the USA and lollies in Australia and New Zealand. These words mean much the same thing, but they come from different places. Sweetmeat is an old-fashioned word for them, so a dictionary is the best way to check it.
fact: A sweetmeat is an old-fashioned word for a sweet, candy or small sweet treat.
fact: Sweetmeats can be sugared fruit, nuts or marzipan.
fact: Sweetmeat has nothing to do with meat, even though it has the word meat in it.
fact: «Meat» once meant any food, so «meat and drink» meant food and drink.
fact: Banquets in Tudor and Victorian times often ended with sweetmeats.
exercise: In an old story, the feast ended with «a plate of sweetmeats». What were the sweetmeats? | Bread and cheese | *Small sweet treats | Cold roast meat | Soup in bowls
exercise: Why is a sweetmeat not a kind of meat? | It is made from the flesh of animals | *It is an old word for a sweet, and meat once meant any food | It is always served cold | It is a kind of soup
exercise: Which modern word for sweets is used in the USA? | *Candy | Sweets | Marzipan | Lollies
test: In the sentence «Words change meaning», what does the example suggest about the word meat? | It has always meant only animal flesh | It means a sweet | It was invented last year | *It once meant any food
test: A child in Auckland asks for sweets. Which word fits her country best? | Candy | *Lollies | Marzipan
exam: The old book says «a plate of sweetmeats» at the feast. Using the clues, what is a sweetmeat? | A savoury pie | A drink served in a cup | *A sweet treat such as sugared fruit, nuts or marzipan | Meat cooked with sugar
